🐛 Describe the bug
inductor/test_torchinductor_dynamic_shapes.py -k test_round_correctness  may fail while inductor/test_torchinductor.py -k test_round_correctness works which is due to rounding of halfway cases, e.g. -8.5 which should be rounded to nearest even (i.e. "-8") but could be rounded to -9 because -ffast-math enables -funsafe-math-optimizations and -fno-rounding-math  which is described as

This flag assumes that the rounding mode is round to nearest.

And indeed on e.g. POWER I was able to reproduce this based on the code torchinductor produces:
#include <iostream>
#include <cmath>
#include <vector>

using T = double;

extern "C" void kernel(const T* in_ptr0,
                       T* out_ptr0,
                       const long ks0)
{
    {
        #pragma GCC ivdep
        for(long i0=static_cast<long>(0L); i0<static_cast<long>(ks0); i0+=static_cast<long>(1L))
        {
            auto tmp0 = in_ptr0[static_cast<long>(i0)];
            auto tmp1 = std::nearbyint(tmp0);
            out_ptr0[static_cast<long>(i0)] = tmp1;
        }
    }
}


int main()
{
    std::vector<T> in(16, -8.5);
    decltype(in) out(in.size());
    kernel(in.data(), out.data(), in.size());
    for(const auto t: out)
        std::cout << t << ", ";
    std::cout << '\n';
}
Compiling this with g++ -O3 -ffast-math  -mcpu=native on PPC yields a series of "-9"s while omitting --ffast-math yields all -8.
I'm wondering what the correct approach about this should be:

Workaround in the test to pass -fno-unsafe-math-optimizations to the compiler to fix the affected test
Unconditionally pass that option on e.g. PPC (and potentially other affected platforms)

Versions
PyTorch 2.1.2
